Z||000000||ChadMan||09-28-2001||10:01 AM||||Toyota will stop producing engines unless CART goes to the same engine format as the IRL (3.5L, no turbo).<P>I honestly don't care who wins the CART/IRL battle, as long as the winning series still features road racing and a few Canadian and/or Mexican races.  Unfortunately, I don't think the IRL will do that if they can help it.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Cheever3000||09-28-2001||11:38 AM||||I'm only interested in IRL because of Eddie, but why did they go with only oval tracks anyway?  Like you, I MUST see some road course racing.<P>About Toyota: heck with em.  Let em leave.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-28-2001||09:43 PM||||CART IRL Battle? yeah, so.... IRL management is mainly comprised of a bunch of whiners.... reminds me of a Baptist church split. You do it this way.... NO! you do it this way.... B_tch, B_tch, B_tch.... until no-one even gives a turd any more. <P>ASA the same way, all they could do was whine how bad attendance was at Dover last time they were here. No-one even knew there was an ASA race that week... who's fault is that besides ASA? NASCAR goes to Dover and they make sure the whole planet knows.<P>CART isn't going away any time soon. Except maybe in the U.S. Let's face it. Besides Sears Point, Watkins Glenn, and maybe one other... what road coarses are there in the north america? Still having the Glenn is some kind of miracle anyway. If Corning hadn't salvaged it when they did it would have been gone for good years ago.<P>IRL comes off like a bunch of NASCAR wannabes. They wish they had half the market pentration of NASCAR and CART.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-29-2001||01:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B> Besides Sears Point, Watkins Glenn, and maybe one other... what road coarses are there in the north america? <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Eh? Lots, Road America, Road Atlanta, Mid Ohio, etc.... <P>I agree the whole thing is just silly, and ends up only turning the fans off.<P>It's a pity, because the racing itself is just better with open-wheel cars.  <P>This is why I love F1 Grand Prix. "Let's get some cars that can pull 4+g turns under downforce, run 240mph, and we'll let them loose IN TOWN!!!" ;')\<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
